---
import StackDiagram from './StackDiagram.astro';
import { REV } from '../../lib/build';
---
<div class="hero-pin" id="heroPin">
<header class="hero wrap" data-sheet="General arrangement" data-n="0">
  <div>
    <p class="dwg r" style="--d:0"><span>DWG-001</span><i></i><span>rev <b>{REV}</b></span><i></i><span>software engineer</span></p>
    <h1 class="r" style="--d:0"><span class="name">Sahil Shahane</span><br><span class="tl">takes systems apart, puts them back <em class="fast">faster.</em></span></h1>
    <p class="typeline r" style="--d:1">
      <span class="tl-label">$</span>
      <span class="tl-out" id="type"
            data-words="billing systems that reconcile;auth that doesn't leak;Kubernetes controllers in Go;a key-value store in Rust;build pipelines 80% faster">billing systems that reconcile</span><span class="caret" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </p>
    <p class="tag r" style="--d:2">
      Currently at <b>IIT Bombay</b>. I care how things actually behave under
      load, not how they're documented to. Most of my work sits a layer below the product —
      billing pipelines, auth, Kubernetes controllers, build tooling — where the problems are
      the ones people tend to call hard. Previously at <b>Outpost Innovations</b> and <b>Sagitec</b>.
    </p>
    <div class="meta r" style="--d:3">
      <a class="chip" href="mailto:sahilpshahane123@gmail.com">
